1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:03,277
You need to build a four-node AHV cluster.

2
00:00:03,627 --> 00:00:06,200
Which Create Cluster workflow should you choose?

3
00:00:06,443 --> 00:00:09,036
Start with the deployment service available at the site.

4
00:00:09,129 --> 00:00:13,523
ZTF-Orchestrator offers three paths to the same goal, but each uses

5
00:00:13,523 --> 00:00:15,592
a different service and configuration.

6
00:00:15,955 --> 00:00:20,563
Choose Cluster Create, Foundation VM, when you have a classic Foundation VM

7
00:00:20,563 --> 00:00:22,292
that can reach the physical nodes.

8
00:00:22,501 --> 00:00:26,461
This suits a local build, a remote site with its own Foundation VM,

9
00:00:26,469 --> 00:00:28,573
or an approved cluster rebuild.

10
00:00:28,773 --> 00:00:33,159
Review the node addresses and credential references, then select the approved
images

11
00:00:33,295 --> 00:00:35,300
already in Foundation inventory.

12
00:00:35,443 --> 00:00:40,086
Refresh inventory, validate the payload, test IPMI credentials and check

13
00:00:40,094 --> 00:00:44,310
progress. The IPMI test uses the Orchestrator's network path;

14
00:00:44,361 --> 00:00:48,734
a failed direct test does not prove Foundation cannot reach the nodes.

15
00:00:48,943 --> 00:00:51,737
Follow Foundation's reported phase and percentage.

16
00:00:52,015 --> 00:00:56,530
Now keep the same four-node requirement, but use Foundation Central associated

17
00:00:56,538 --> 00:01:00,506
with Prism Central. Choose the workflow named Cluster Create.

18
00:01:00,693 --> 00:01:04,867
It uses the existing ZTF one point x execution path.

19
00:01:05,088 --> 00:01:09,432
Configure the Foundation Central endpoint and credentials, then review eligible

20
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,745
discovered nodes and the approved images.

21
00:01:12,018 --> 00:01:16,029
This is the appropriate choice when your deployment service and node inventory are

22
00:01:16,029 --> 00:01:19,118
already managed through that Foundation Central environment.

23
00:01:19,388 --> 00:01:23,689
If your deployment service is a separate Foundation Central Appliance, choose Cluster

24
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:26,100
Create, Standalone FCA.

25
00:01:26,428 --> 00:01:29,485
This path uses the appliance's Lifecycle APIs.

26
00:01:29,699 --> 00:01:34,000
Check the actual API version, inventory and hardware compatibility before

27
00:01:34,051 --> 00:01:38,480
proceeding. Submission remains guarded and requires the explicit execution

28
00:01:38,488 --> 00:01:42,815
acknowledgement. A workflow being available does not establish compatibility

29
00:01:42,865 --> 00:01:45,147
with every appliance or hardware version.

30
00:01:45,511 --> 00:01:48,468
For each path, use its matching YAML schema.

31
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:51,529
Do not swap configuration files between services.

32
00:01:51,803 --> 00:01:55,848
Run the checks available in that workflow, review the exact physical targets

33
00:01:55,899 --> 00:01:58,494
and obtain the required approval before imaging.

34
00:01:58,715 --> 00:02:01,416
Imaging can overwrite existing installations.

35
00:02:01,851 --> 00:02:06,515
Monitor the submitted job and inspect the real outcome before retrying a failure.

36
00:02:06,629 --> 00:02:11,144
After cluster formation, verify Prism Element and continue with the reviewed

37
00:02:11,152 --> 00:02:12,988
post-configuration pipeline.

38
00:02:13,175 --> 00:02:17,832
Prism Central registration, when needed, is a separate configuration step.

39
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:22,733
For a broader site or multiple-cluster deployment, review Site Deploy or Site

40
00:02:22,733 --> 00:02:25,071
Deploy, Standalone FCA.

41
00:02:25,293 --> 00:02:28,216
Imaging Only prepares nodes without forming a cluster.

42
00:02:28,424 --> 00:02:33,024
For our four-node example, choose the Create Cluster workflow that matches the
service

43
00:02:33,075 --> 00:02:34,640
you actually operate.
